WEBVTT

00:15.560 --> 00:18.390
I never dreamed before

00:18.390 --> 00:21.230
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.230 --> 00:24.800
into the world of perfect free

00:24.800 --> 00:26.900
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:26.900 --> 00:29.740
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.740 --> 00:32.470
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.470 --> 00:36.040
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.040 --> 00:37.210
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.210 --> 00:40.120
I was made to hit in America

00:40.120 --> 00:42.980
(I was made to hit in America)

00:42.980 --> 00:48.890
I was made to hit in America

00:48.890 --> 00:52.560
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.560 --> 00:54.560
(To me, forever)

00:54.560 --> 00:58.270
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.270 --> 01:01.200
(To me, forever)

01:08.340 --> 01:13.950
I was made to hit in America

01:13.950 --> 01:16.790
I was made to hit in America

01:16.790 --> 01:19.650
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.650 --> 01:22.460
I was made to hit in America

01:22.460 --> 01:25.230
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.230 --> 01:32.860
I was made to hit in America

01:37.540 --> 01:39.730
Oh well...

01:46.850 --> 01:49.280
Stop...

01:49.280 --> 01:56.750
Stop!

02:12.210 --> 02:14.580
Koyuki is the best!

02:14.580 --> 02:15.680
Have you lost your mind?

02:15.680 --> 02:17.710
What the hell are you saying
all of a sudden?

02:17.710 --> 02:21.650
I said Koyuki is the best.

02:21.650 --> 02:24.820
The vocalist for your band's
gotta be Koyuki.

02:24.820 --> 02:30.390
He's a genius. He's gonna
be a fucking great vocalist.

02:30.390 --> 02:34.900
Hey, we're not talking about
making the choir here, understand?

02:34.900 --> 02:38.000
Now really, you don't understand!

02:38.000 --> 02:41.940
What are they fighting about?
I can't understand them at all.

02:41.940 --> 02:44.110
I think Koyuki will be great too!

02:44.110 --> 02:45.400
Huh?!

02:48.410 --> 02:53.650
The vocalist for the band.
I think Koyuki will be good!

02:53.650 --> 02:55.240
Vocalist?

02:58.750 --> 03:01.810
Koyuki and Chiba, huh?

03:06.960 --> 03:10.660
W-what? What're you looking at?!

04:08.350 --> 04:12.680
Yukio! You have a letter from Hiro-kun!

04:13.950 --> 04:16.960
"How are you, Yukio-kun?
I'm doing very well right now."

04:16.960 --> 04:20.960
"I won the Kyushu
Piano Contest the other day!"

04:20.960 --> 04:23.960
"Do you know how big that is?
I might even go to Vienna!"

04:23.960 --> 04:25.930
"P.S. I bought the latest Sangokushi."

04:31.410 --> 04:33.210
Let's see...

04:33.210 --> 04:36.040
"Dear Hiro-kun,"

04:36.040 --> 04:42.880
"Thank you for your letter.
I've started playing the guitar."

04:42.880 --> 04:48.060
"It's surprisingly easy to play."

04:48.060 --> 04:51.790
"I've mastered music played
by Van Halen, Steve Vai,

04:51.790 --> 05:04.070
Paul Gilbert, Nuno, Zakk Wylde,
and even Yot-chan..."

05:04.070 --> 05:08.310
"I'm practicing
'The Song of the Seasons' right now."

05:08.310 --> 05:13.980
"Wouldn't it be great if we
could play together in Vienna?"

05:13.980 --> 05:20.790
"The photo I've enclosed was taken
at the East Japan Guitar Awards

05:20.790 --> 05:23.990
held at the municipal gymnasium."

05:23.990 --> 05:29.200
"It's from when I won in
the middle school division."

05:29.200 --> 05:30.820
"Yours truly..."

05:35.270 --> 05:38.900
Mom, I'm going to the gymnasium!

06:08.900 --> 06:11.670
What am I doing anyway?

06:23.320 --> 06:27.250
It's almost summer vacation...

06:32.560 --> 06:36.090
All right! First, I'm gonna
find me a giant beetle!

07:13.170 --> 07:21.810
Today's cloudy skies
will clear up with time

07:21.810 --> 07:27.110
Go for it, don't be tied down,
set yourself free

07:27.110 --> 07:33.850
Feel free, yes,
the new tomorrow is wow wow

07:35.220 --> 07:41.460
So cheer up,
because I want to see your smile

07:59.950 --> 08:01.940
H-hello...

08:08.760 --> 08:10.950
I-I'm sorry!

08:12.360 --> 08:15.060
Who was that kid?

08:15.060 --> 08:17.000
Koyuki.

08:17.000 --> 08:21.540
-About time you leave.
-Huh? Forget that kid.

08:21.540 --> 08:23.540
Go home!

08:23.540 --> 08:25.940
He's more important than me?

08:25.940 --> 08:26.940
Yeah.

08:26.940 --> 08:32.970
You felt differently yesterday!
You were so nice yesterday...

08:34.180 --> 08:36.270
You're the pits!

08:43.160 --> 08:45.060
-Yo!
-I-I'm sorry!

08:45.060 --> 08:49.330
Granny's not here now.
Let's practice a song.

08:49.330 --> 08:51.800
Ryusuke-kun...I...

08:51.800 --> 08:54.500
I have to talk to you.

08:54.500 --> 08:56.770
What is it?

09:17.720 --> 09:19.750
Get the fuck outta here!

09:30.970 --> 09:34.130
Never come around again.

09:36.940 --> 09:38.880
I'm so sorry!

09:51.530 --> 09:55.460
I'm sorry...I'm sorry...

09:56.300 --> 10:00.630
I'm sorry...I'm sorry!

10:00.630 --> 10:02.300
I'm sorry...

10:44.950 --> 10:46.510
All right!

10:46.510 --> 10:51.290
First, get the lane markers
and we'll go 200 meters four times!

10:51.290 --> 10:54.150
-Are you serious?!
-We'll die!

10:54.150 --> 10:56.260
I won't allow any slacking!

10:56.260 --> 11:02.660
This summer, we're gonna get
way better than the rival schools!

11:02.660 --> 11:05.930
Umm...What about my plans
as team advisor?

11:10.600 --> 11:13.270
Boy, that interim coach is tough.

11:13.270 --> 11:17.210
It's only been two weeks,
but he's way more than interim!

11:17.210 --> 11:22.480
If this keeps up, everyone will
quit the team! But he sure is tough!

11:22.480 --> 11:28.190
Saito-san is a fanatic who swims
over 30,000 meters every week!

11:28.190 --> 11:31.690
It's like, is he really 44?!

11:31.690 --> 11:36.000
By the way, isn't Koyuki-kun
joining the team?

11:36.000 --> 11:39.630
He's in a bit of a bind right now.

11:39.630 --> 11:43.740
-Bind?
-Yeah.

11:43.740 --> 11:46.400
I wonder if he's okay.

11:48.940 --> 11:53.080
Hey, you two girls! No slacking!

11:53.080 --> 11:54.710
-Sorry!
-Sorry!

12:09.930 --> 12:13.230
Yukio, you have a letter from Hiro-kun!

12:16.740 --> 12:18.210
"I'm shocked you started
playing the guitar."

12:18.210 --> 12:20.710
"But I bet you're still
no match for my piano skills."

12:20.710 --> 12:23.210
"I wanna hear how good you are.
Play for me whenever I visit next."

12:23.210 --> 12:26.580
"P.S. I didn't get to go to Vienna,
but I did visit Holland Town."

12:52.440 --> 12:57.080
Huh? Koyuki-kun, right?

12:57.080 --> 12:58.580
Yes.

12:58.580 --> 13:02.980
Did something happen? I haven't
seen you at the pool since then.

13:02.980 --> 13:04.350
No.

13:04.350 --> 13:06.350
You play the guitar?

13:06.350 --> 13:09.220
Err...no...

13:10.990 --> 13:15.500
-This is...
-Oh boy, that's bad!

13:15.500 --> 13:17.900
Yes...

13:17.900 --> 13:20.300
Once it's broken...

13:20.300 --> 13:24.600
Broken things can't be fixed.

13:24.600 --> 13:27.040
-I wonder about that.
-Huh?

13:27.040 --> 13:30.440
This guitar can probably be fixed.

13:30.440 --> 13:35.380
My friend will do it for cheap.
Give it a month and it'll be fixed.

13:36.450 --> 13:37.940
It can be fixed?

13:40.550 --> 13:42.080
Saito-san...

13:43.320 --> 13:48.430
I may not look like it,
but British rock changed my life.

13:48.430 --> 13:50.400
Saito-san...

13:50.400 --> 13:54.670
Poor guitar, if you throw it away.

13:54.670 --> 13:57.800
Come on over anytime,
and bring that guitar.

13:59.640 --> 14:02.870
If you'd like, I'd be happy to teach you.

14:05.080 --> 14:06.140
See you!

14:13.690 --> 14:15.210
All right.

14:31.910 --> 14:34.510
This is pitiful...

14:34.510 --> 14:36.810
About Koyuki...

14:39.450 --> 14:44.180
That guitar was given to me by Eddie.

14:44.180 --> 14:46.790
No one would give me the time of day...

14:46.790 --> 14:51.590
And it was Eddie who took the time
to talk to this Japanese kid.

14:51.590 --> 14:53.650
But even Koyuki...

14:56.830 --> 14:58.330
Ryusuke-kun...

14:58.330 --> 15:01.100
Hey! Look, look!

15:08.480 --> 15:11.270
Look what I got!

15:13.580 --> 15:16.740
-Hey, Ryusuke! Help me!
-Huh?

15:18.550 --> 15:22.090
Here you are, Izumi-chan!

15:22.090 --> 15:23.790
Oh, thanks...

15:23.790 --> 15:27.160
-Don't mention it!
-Huh? What about for me?

15:27.160 --> 15:30.230
-It was hilarious the other day...
-Huh?
-Huh?

15:30.230 --> 15:33.270
Ryusuke's never eaten natto in his life.

15:33.270 --> 15:35.940
-Huh?! You serious?!
-So

15:35.940 --> 15:37.900
Hey. It's almost time.

15:37.900 --> 15:39.370
-Right.
-Right.

15:39.370 --> 15:41.310
Man, who cares about the concert?

15:41.310 --> 15:45.950
-Don't you want to make
summer memories with me?
-Let's go!

15:45.950 --> 15:51.410
Hey! I'm coming, too! C'mon!
It'd be the perfect double date!

16:24.320 --> 16:26.920
Can't think of a band without him.

16:26.920 --> 16:29.910
Yeah, definitely funky.

16:44.700 --> 16:48.980
Man, the vocals were terrible!

16:48.980 --> 16:50.110
What the hell-?!

16:50.110 --> 16:55.380
With vocals like that,
I feel sorry for Taira.

16:55.380 --> 16:56.720
Why you-!

16:56.720 --> 16:58.720
Good evening, everyone!

16:58.720 --> 17:03.420
I'm Manabu and I used to
do vocals with The Crowd!

17:03.420 --> 17:06.930
-Manabu!
-Sing for us!

17:06.930 --> 17:08.560
You're so cool!

17:08.560 --> 17:10.860
Switch with me, you're terrible.

17:13.600 --> 17:15.630
Why you-!

17:20.010 --> 17:22.240
Sing, Manabu!

17:23.910 --> 17:25.110
Ryusuke-kun...

17:25.110 --> 17:28.620
I know. This was Eiji's idea.

17:28.620 --> 17:32.550
Well, since I'm on stage,
maybe I'll sing.

17:32.550 --> 17:35.720
The Music Men are here,

17:35.720 --> 17:40.350
so maybe I'll sing "Journey"
by the Heartbreakers!

17:44.430 --> 17:46.730
What'll we do?

17:46.730 --> 17:48.670
Hurry and sing!

18:02.950 --> 18:07.990
Who's calling my name?
I hear the voice of legends

18:07.990 --> 18:14.290
What do I want?
Static emotion comes down

18:14.290 --> 18:19.600
Did I have the dream?
Am I misunderstood?

18:19.600 --> 18:25.570
What do I want?
Static emotion comes down

18:25.570 --> 18:28.270
-I'm going home.
-What?

18:28.270 --> 18:31.300
I don't know what's good about him at all.

18:44.160 --> 18:47.960
"Saito Paper Company"

18:47.960 --> 18:50.630
"Saito Paper Company"

18:47.960 --> 18:50.630

That's it! F is played by
pressing down with your index finger.

18:50.630 --> 18:53.330
That's it! F is played by
pressing down with your index finger.

18:54.500 --> 18:56.870
Hmm...pretty good.

18:56.870 --> 18:58.340
Really?

18:58.340 --> 19:02.210
You're progressing nicely.
You can make sounds now.

19:02.210 --> 19:04.510
Yeah.

19:04.510 --> 19:07.480
Now that you've gotten
the hang of common chords,

19:07.480 --> 19:10.420
let's try to play continuously.

19:10.420 --> 19:12.750
Uhh...My fingers...

19:12.750 --> 19:14.890
Hurt, don't they?

19:14.890 --> 19:18.220
But if you give up now,
you won't make it with girls.

19:18.220 --> 19:21.230
No, that's not what I-

19:21.230 --> 19:23.860
Koyuki-kun. Observe.

19:27.400 --> 19:29.490
T-that's amazing!

19:31.370 --> 19:33.570
Koyuki-kun, come with me.

19:33.570 --> 19:35.010
Okay.

19:46.890 --> 19:49.520
When I got injured and had
my Olympic dreams shattered,

19:49.520 --> 19:53.250
I felt so sorry for myself,
and my only consolation...

19:59.470 --> 20:01.300
...was guitars!

20:01.300 --> 20:04.200
Which one do you like, Koyuki-kun?

20:08.040 --> 20:11.340
The guitar on the left is
the same shape as Ryusuke-kun's!

20:11.340 --> 20:16.280
Oh...I'll bet that one
is a Gibson Les Paul.

20:16.280 --> 20:20.290
But mine is a fake
called the Tibson Les Paul.

20:20.290 --> 20:25.250
When it was 360 yen to the dollar,
I couldn't afford the real McCoy.

20:26.390 --> 20:28.430
Tibson?

20:28.430 --> 20:31.600
Now then...I'll let you
borrow this Les Paul.

20:31.600 --> 20:33.570
Huh?! Are you sure?!

20:33.570 --> 20:38.670
You'll also need a tuning machine,
and...an amp.

20:38.670 --> 20:45.040
Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool!

20:45.040 --> 20:46.110
"My name is Page."

20:45.040 --> 20:46.110

Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool!

20:46.110 --> 20:47.850
"My name is Page."

20:46.110 --> 20:47.850

-Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool!
-Page?

20:47.850 --> 20:52.120
Ever heard of a band
called the Rocket Boys?

20:52.120 --> 20:53.550
Fool!

20:53.550 --> 20:57.860
They're a mystery British group,
overshadowed by the Beatles,

20:57.860 --> 21:00.790
who recorded one album
and then broke up.

21:00.790 --> 21:03.320
They're the teachers of my soul.

21:07.930 --> 21:10.400
Follow me

21:10.400 --> 21:15.710
Baby, I won't let you leave
if you believe in me

21:15.710 --> 21:18.650
-And I always set you free
from all those yesteryears


21:15.710 --> 21:18.650
-A-amazing!

21:18.650 --> 21:20.380
-And I always set you free
from all those yesteryears


21:18.650 --> 21:20.380
-I've never seen a bird like that,

21:20.380 --> 21:22.180
even on TV.

21:22.180 --> 21:23.020
That's Page.

21:23.020 --> 21:28.550
The one and only friend of Kenichi Saito,
age 44 and unmarried.

21:34.930 --> 21:36.130
Fool!

21:36.130 --> 21:39.860
Making him sing is my goal.

21:59.450 --> 22:01.220
Dammit!

22:02.890 --> 22:06.380
He'll only respond to great music!

22:07.560 --> 22:12.430
Koyuki-kun! Let's do our best
to make Page sing!

22:12.430 --> 22:15.470
All right! If I'm going to try,
I may as well give it my best!

22:15.470 --> 22:17.500
That's the spirit, Koyuki-kun!

22:17.500 --> 22:20.770
Just wait! We'll make him sing for us!

22:20.770 --> 22:23.780
Yes! Atta boy, Koyuki-kun!

22:23.780 --> 22:27.080
Of the three feudal generals,
I like Nobunaga the best.

22:29.780 --> 22:31.580
Fool!

22:31.580 --> 22:33.950
Okay then, let's start today's practice!

22:33.950 --> 22:36.220
All right! Please teach me!

22:36.220 --> 22:37.860
A!

22:37.860 --> 22:39.530
D!

22:39.530 --> 22:41.060
G!

22:41.060 --> 22:42.550
F!

22:50.240 --> 22:52.340
Another minute

22:52.340 --> 22:55.280
Feelin' so fine

22:57.350 --> 22:59.580
You turn the freeze

22:59.580 --> 23:02.410
into warm light

23:04.420 --> 23:07.990
Had a premonition

23:07.990 --> 23:10.690
I've been waitin' ever since

23:10.690 --> 23:14.200
My world comin' down

23:14.200 --> 23:16.720
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:18.770 --> 23:25.110
If you really wanna fly

23:25.110 --> 23:27.870
you gotta let go

23:39.960 --> 23:42.290
Simply the most

23:42.290 --> 23:44.330
big sensation

23:44.330 --> 23:47.130
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:47.130 --> 23:49.400
She's really pretty

23:49.400 --> 23:51.470
One-eyed vision

23:51.470 --> 23:54.240
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:54.240 --> 23:57.910
Little sister showed me

23:57.910 --> 24:00.540
Really took me for a ride

24:00.540 --> 24:02.140
My world comin' down

24:02.140 --> 24:05.610
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:05.610 --> 24:09.350
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:13.820 --> 24:16.160
The road comes to a fork.

24:16.160 --> 24:16.690
"Next Episode"

24:16.160 --> 24:16.690

The road comes to a fork.

24:16.690 --> 24:20.090
"Next Episode"


24:16.690 --> 24:20.090
Isn't love so painful?
